<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">French invasion of Russia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1812</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Patriotic War of 1812 · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The French invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s campaign of 1812, known in Russia as the Patriotic War. The Russian army retreated, fought at Borodino, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> burned after its occupation; Napoleon's retreat in winter destroyed most of his army, a turning point that raised the prestige of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/french-invasion-of-russia.jpg" alt="French invasion of Russia" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Albrecht Adam · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IV_corpo_durante_la_campagna_di_Russia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
